# DubFlow environment variables. Copy to .env (never commit it) and edit.
#   Windows: set them in PowerShell before scripts/start.ps1 (the defaults below already match the Windows layout).
#   Linux:   scripts/start-linux.sh loads .env automatically. Unset variables fall back to the defaults shown in the Linux column.
#
# Variable                  | Windows example (default on Windows)                              | Linux example (default on Linux)
# --------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------+------------------------------------------------------
# DUBFLOW_DATA_DIR          | D:/DuAnKhoiNghiep/DubFlow/data                                    | /srv/dubflow/data            (default <repo>/data)
# DUBFLOW_RUNTIME_DIR       | (not used)                                                        | /srv/dubflow/runtime         (default <repo>/runtime)
# DUBFLOW_MODELS_DIR        | (not used)                                                        | /srv/dubflow/models          (default <repo>/models)
# DUBFLOW_FFMPEG            | D:/OmniVoice/tools/ffmpeg.exe                                     | /usr/bin/ffmpeg              (default: ffmpeg on PATH)
# DUBFLOW_FFPROBE           | D:/OmniVoice/tools/ffprobe.exe                                    | /usr/bin/ffprobe             (default: ffprobe on PATH)
# DUBFLOW_ASR_PYTHON        | D:/OmniVoice/venv/Scripts/python.exe                              | <runtime>/asr/.venv/bin/python
# DUBFLOW_TTS_PYTHON        | <repo>/repo-tests/clone-voxcpm/Scripts/python.exe                 | <runtime>/tts/.venv/bin/python
# DUBFLOW_OCR_PYTHON        | <repo>/repo-tests/ocr/Scripts/python.exe                          | <runtime>/ocr/.venv/bin/python
# DUBFLOW_SPEAKER_PYTHON    | <repo>/repo-tests/speaker-runtime/Scripts/python.exe              | <runtime>/speaker/.venv/bin/python
# DUBFLOW_MODEL_CACHE       | <repo>/repo-tests/runtime/hf-cache      (VoxCPM2)                 | <models>/cache/hf-tts
# DUBFLOW_ASR_CACHE         | D:/OmniVoice/cache/hf                   (Whisper, OmniVoice)      | <models>/cache/hf-asr
# DUBFLOW_LAMA_MODEL        | <repo>/models/lama/lama_fp32.onnx                                 | <models>/lama/lama_fp32.onnx
# DUBFLOW_CUDA_DLL_DIR      | D:/OmniVoice/venv/Lib/site-packages/torch/lib                     | (leave empty; Linux uses the system CUDA libraries)
# DUBFLOW_SYSTEM_VOICES     | D:/OmniVoice/voices                                               | <models>/voices
# DUBFLOW_VI_PROMPT         | <repo>/bench/runs/20261027/refs-origreview/vi-prompt.json         | <models>/vi-prompt/vi-prompt.json (+ vi-prompt.wav next to it)
# DUBFLOW_SPEAKER_MODEL     | <repo>/repo-tests/models/speaker-ecapa-voxceleb (fallback)        | <models>/speaker-ecapa-voxceleb
# TORCH_HOME                | (set by scripts/local-test-env.ps1)                               | <models>/cache/torch  (Demucs checkpoint: hub/checkpoints/955717e8-8726e21a.th)
# DUBFLOW_VIDEO_ENCODER     | auto | nvenc | libx264                                           | auto | libx264 (use libx264 without an NVENC-capable ffmpeg)
# DUBFLOW_REDIS_URL         | (empty = durable local SQLite queue)                              | (empty)
#
# Linux example:
# DUBFLOW_DATA_DIR=/srv/dubflow/data
# DUBFLOW_MODELS_DIR=/srv/dubflow/models
# DUBFLOW_RUNTIME_DIR=/srv/dubflow/runtime
#
# Windows values (commented out so a copy of this file is safe on Linux; PowerShell users set these as $env:NAME):
# DUBFLOW_DATA_DIR=D:/DuAnKhoiNghiep/DubFlow/data
# DUBFLOW_FFMPEG=D:/OmniVoice/tools/ffmpeg.exe
# DUBFLOW_FFPROBE=D:/OmniVoice/tools/ffprobe.exe
# DUBFLOW_ASR_PYTHON=D:/OmniVoice/venv/Scripts/python.exe
# DUBFLOW_TTS_PYTHON=D:/DuAnKhoiNghiep/DubFlow/repo-tests/clone-voxcpm/Scripts/python.exe
# DUBFLOW_OCR_PYTHON=D:/DuAnKhoiNghiep/DubFlow/repo-tests/ocr/Scripts/python.exe
# DUBFLOW_MODEL_CACHE=D:/DuAnKhoiNghiep/DubFlow/repo-tests/runtime/hf-cache
# DUBFLOW_ASR_CACHE=D:/OmniVoice/cache/hf
# Leave empty for durable local SQLite queue. RQ requires a separate worker.
DUBFLOW_REDIS_URL=
